<div id="2026-09-11-traveler-queue-remainder" class="cl-entry">
<h3>2026-09-11 — Traveler "Add to Print Queue" now queues only the true remainder</h3>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>What.</strong> Changed the traveler's queue action so it creates <strong>one</strong> queue entry per part carrying exactly the remaining shortfall, never double-queueing. Logic moved into <code>Traveler-&gt;queue_part_print</code>: <code>remainder = qty_needed - on_hand - already_queued</code>. If the remainder is &le; 0 it returns <code>{ok=&gt;1, queued=&gt;0, message=&gt;'No remainder to queue…'}</code> instead of adding a redundant job. The traveler button now passes <code>part.qty_needed</code> (not the old <code>queue_qty||qty_short</code>), and the JS shows the "nothing left to queue" message when the need is already covered by stock + existing queue.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Why.</strong> Previously the button queued the raw shortfall and ignored what was already in the queue, so clicking twice (or queueing a part that was partially queued) created duplicate jobs. Per the user's rule: one queue entry per item, qty = need - stock - already-queued; remainder only.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Printer assignment stays with the queue, not the traveler.</strong> The traveler remains printer-agnostic. Next-available-printer auto-assign is explicitly deferred until the between-print maintenance ritual is reliable (see printer-maintenance doc). The <code>Printing3dJob.printer_id</code> column already exists but is not yet populated by queueing.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Files.</strong> <code>lib/Comserv/Util/Manufacturing/Traveler.pm</code> (remainder math in <code>queue_part_print</code>), <code>root/Accounting/Manufacturing/traveler_view.tt</code> (button passes qty_needed; JS handles the no-remainder case). <code>perl -c</code> OK. NOTE: the <code>.pm</code> change needs the :4003 server to reload the module to take effect; the <code>.tt</code> changes are live on next request.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Docs.</strong> Added "5.1 Printer Maintenance (between-print, per printer type)" to <code>features/3d_printing.tt</code>: universal pre-next-print checklist + per-type table (Anycubic LAN-mode manual hour tracking since the cloud 500h tracker is offline; Bambu/AMS; resin/SLA). Flags the open items: no automated maintenance tracker yet; auto-assign deferred.</p>
</div>
